514081/state-v-laney/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: State v. Laney\">654 S. W. 2d 383</a></span>; No. 83-5544, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9471084\"><a href=\"/opinion/424005/john-eldon-smith-v-ralph-m-kemp-superintendent-georgia-diagnostic/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: John Eldon Smith v. Ralph M. Kemp, Superintendent,...\">715 F. 2d 1459</a></span>; No. 83-5644, <span class=\"citation multiple-matches\"><a href=\"/c/F.%202d/706/1534/\">706 F. 2d 1534</a></span>.</p>\n</opinion>"},{"id":9282139,"type":"dissent","typeCode":"040dissent","perCuriam":false,"author":"Brennanmarshall","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":597,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"dissent\">\n<author id=\"b877-10\">Justice Brennan and Justice Marshall,</author>\n<p id=\"AQVM\">dissenting.</p>\n<p id=\"b877-11\">Adhering to our views that the death penalty is in all circumstances cruel and unusual punishment prohibited by the Eighth and Fourteenth Amendments, <em>Gregg </em>v. <em>Georgia, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9426555\"><a href=\"/opinion/109532/gregg-v-georgia/#227\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Gregg v. Georgia\">428 U. S. 153, 227, 231</a></span> (1976), we would grant certiorari and vacate the death sentences in these cases.</p>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}